 " returns."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"955ca1a1-72ae-48fe-8ebb-90cb19c9f211"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the legacy compatibility spelling. New code uses ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraHalfLineQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519b108f-fba3-4274-9f04-d75d66a5297f"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5572dfee-3c67-4514-bf9c-c0678020aaa9"],

Cell["\<\
Two conditions, and the asymmetry between them is the whole definition:\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e84ddc1d-8ec5-450e-b496-3e75fb1cd217"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "b27bac54-3d1e-4a23-86eb-17c4a90d2261"], Cell["Condition", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"b5485d44-2eb1-43bf-83ad-7e2486e16a1b"],
     Cell["Why", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"31ff5a3f-8cdc-4db7-8ea6-26fee40b923f"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ae1a5392-7baf-4d22-bf57-1ed238df93d5"], Cell[
    "the sequence is a shortest path", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7ff9a101-d5bc-416d-abbe-758568a7c291"], Cell[TextData[{
     "a ray is straight, so ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      TemplateBox[{
        Cell[
         TextData["InfraSegmentQ"]], 
        "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegmentQ", 
        "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
       "PackageLink",
       BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "9e1c81aa-7a52-4393-b683-aff67684b447"],
     " must hold"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"672ad368-0e80-45ff-bfe9-120d34be0270"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "9f1d2440-1994-4804-a6f4-1e8621b443d7"], Cell["\<\
no neighbour of the last vertex sits one step farther from the first\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"503e6e64-2c82-43ed-a73a-b2268351aab5"], 
    Cell["the far end is inextensible", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2a6aef18-5ad1-493f-942f-52c46e3df53c"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"c2c67ef3-34a1-44fd-9ad0-\
6253cb30d11b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inextensibility is required ",
 StyleBox["only at the far end",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The origin is an endpoint by fiat \[LongDash] that is exactly what \
distinguishes a ray from a line (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraLineQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraLineQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6c1162e5-fbe0-4cda-9616-e95b29be09a8"],
 " asks for inextensibility at both ends), and it means a ray may start \
anywhere, not only at a peripheral vertex."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f6e7a5d4-bcd0-40a2-8141-df512c5bc645"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sequences shorter than two vertices are ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6385cfd-a76a-4061-8f29-4b3d9bbfd613"],
 ": a single vertex has no direction."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5e091b75-e1c7-441a-996c-00e63fe43051"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicate is the companion of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraRay"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraRay", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3276af54-1054-45b5-afc9-8a95454704ed"],
 ", which prolongs a shortest path outward until no neighbour prolongs it, so \
every ray that finder returns satisfies it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"26cc5f59-a52f-474f-b586-d70668aee802"]
}, Open  ]],

